From aa89ad34894f4b6d561d93c43a69804b069db583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 10:32:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deep-link): open prefilled patrol editor from
 myra://patrol/new links

Extend the myra:// deep-link handler to recognize
`myra://patrol/new?template=<id>` (the landing site's "Open in Myra" links)
and route the main window to the prefilled patrol editor
(`/schedules/edit/?template=<id>`), alongside the existing auth-callback link.

- lib.rs: add `parse_patrol_template` (charset-restricted id), buffer the
  target in `PendingNavigation` for the cold-start case, emit the existing
  `tray-navigate` event, and expose `take_pending_navigation`.
- tray-action-listener: drain the buffered navigation on mount.
- schedule-ideas: enable the ready "Popular" template group (dailyBrief,
  standupPrep, weeklyReview) so multiple deep links resolve to real templates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013YqsGjXbSBoqDCqtxNtZiT
